From 20e38fcac89dc24f3d4a182d1fb3b559d2e0ffa7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: legsmechanical <joshgaine@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 3 Jun 2026 15:18:34 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] feat(fx): generic FX bus editor serving Master + Send A/B

Genericize the Master FX UI into one bus-descriptor-driven editor
(FX_BUS: master/sendA/sendB) and route Send A/B through it instead of
the old minimal send screen. Sends get the full editor (slots, module
browser, bypass, preset UI) minus LFOs (hasLfo:false gates both the LFO
menu items and the LFO indicator draw).

- Route the FX bus picker and slot-list entries through enterFxBusEditor,
  which sets activeFxBus before entering the shared MASTER_FX view.
- Master slot-list entry now also goes through enterFxBusEditor so it
  resets the active bus (prevents a stale send descriptor leaking in).
- Send module param editor returns to the generic editor view.
- Delete shadow_ui_send_fx.mjs and all its dead dispatch/import/ctx wiring;
  keep enterSendFxHierarchyEditor (the generic editor uses it for sends).

Send preset save/load and the Volume (return level) item render but no-op
until the C-side Checkpoint B lands.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
